--TEST--
`delete` names one job, so it is asked with the receipt and never with the queue that receipt carries — `rule:concurrency/queue-deletion-is-explicit-and-bounded`, `rule:core-api/shape-rules`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The two removal members are told apart by their subject and by nothing else:
// this one names *one* job, so it takes the receipt whole, and the queue it
// removes from is the one the receipt was written with. Its sibling is the
// member asked about a queue, and taking a name here would leave two spellings
// of "remove from this queue" differing only in how much they remove.
var $receipt = Core\Queue::push("jobs/send-receipt.nvs");
bool $gone = Core\Queue::delete($receipt);

// So the queue name is not a subject this member has, even though it is the
// name the grant is matched against — that name arrives inside the receipt.
bool $swept = Core\Queue::delete("email");
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `Core\Queue\Id`, found `string`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
